{
  "key": "jo_desto_correlatives",
  "concept_slug": "jo_desto_correlatives",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Using jo and desto for Proportional Change",
  "cefr_level": "B2",
  "goal": "Use jo ... desto and jo ... jo to say that one change increases or decreases with another.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": "obj_pattern",
      "statement": "Recognize the fixed comparative correlative pattern jo + comparative, desto or jo + comparative.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_order",
      "statement": "Place the subject and finite verb correctly in both halves of a jo ... desto sentence.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_transfer",
      "statement": "Avoid English-like transfer such as the more ... the more in Norwegian.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_produce",
      "statement": "Build natural Bokmål sentences that express proportional change with jo ... desto or jo ... jo.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_000",
      "role": "orient",
      "objective_ids": [],
      "title": "What the Pattern Does",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo ... desto",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " when two changes move together: as one thing becomes more, less, better, earlier, and so on, another thing changes too. English often uses the more ... the more. Norwegian does not translate the two the words directly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The fixed pattern is "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + comparative, then "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "desto",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + comparative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo mer du øver, desto bedre blir uttalen din."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The more you practise, the better your pronunciation becomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo tidligere vi starter, desto roligere blir dagen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The earlier we start, the calmer the day becomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A comparative is a form that compares, such as better, earlier, more clearly, or less expensive. In Norwegian, the comparative can be one word like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "bedre",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or a phrase like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "mer effektivt",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_001",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_pattern"
      ],
      "title": "The Two Halves",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A full sentence has two clauses: two groups with a subject and a finite verb. A finite verb is the verb that shows tense, such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "leser",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ble",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "har",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". The first half starts with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " plus the comparative. The second half starts with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "desto",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or another "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " plus the comparative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "en",
            "no",
            "en"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Half"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Norwegian pattern"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Role"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "First half"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Jo + comparative + subject + finite verb"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Sets the condition or scale"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Second half"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "desto + comparative + finite verb + subject"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Gives the result on the same scale"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Alternative second half"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "jo + comparative + finite verb + subject"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Also correct, often a little more compact"
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo mer hun leste, desto lettere forsto hun teksten."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The more she read, the more easily she understood the text."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo mindre sukker du bruker, jo friskere smaker sausen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The less sugar you use, the fresher the sauce tastes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "In the second half, the comparative phrase comes first, so the finite verb normally comes before the subject: "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "desto bedre blir du",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", not "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "desto bedre du blir",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " when it is a complete main result clause."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_002",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_pattern"
      ],
      "title": "Common Transfer Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "English invites a direct copy of the more ... the more. Norwegian uses the fixed correlative words "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "jo",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "desto",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not a repeated word for the."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Do not use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "den mer",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "det mer",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " to mean the more in this pattern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo mer presist du forklarer problemet, desto raskere kan vi løse det."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The more precisely you explain the problem, the faster we can solve it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jo flere eksempler du ser, jo tryggere blir mønsteret."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The more examples you see, the more familiar the pattern becomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Keep this separate from ordinary uses of "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "jo",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " as a stance particle meaning something like as you know. In this pattern, "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "jo",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " is part of a fixed comparative structure."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
